WEBVTT

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.600
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.930
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.140
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:19.670
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:29.920
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.350
Go! Go!

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:36.730
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.630
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.000
Always in the good days in my life!

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:50.000
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.380
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.820
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.950
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.430
is a memory I carry with me.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.790
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.160
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.560
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.470
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.190
Wh-Who the hell are you, you insolent barbarian?!

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.830
Ow! What's the big idea?!

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.040
So, you're Kotaro, huh? I guess I expected too much.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.630
C-CUT IT OUT! Who the hell are you?!

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.670
The commando has come! The commando is resolute!

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.500
All right! I've been waiting for this!

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.840
The wandering president of Cyberdyne who proclaims there is no need for heaven OR earth!

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.140
COMMANDO Z has arrived!

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.830
You're the world's greatest, Mr. President!

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.360
Of course I am! Yay!

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.320
World's greatest, my ass!

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.530
Look, Commando Pepper or Spicy or whatever, but the name Nanbara—

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.070
That's my true name as well.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.590
Surname: Nanbara.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.580
Given name: Totaro.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.060
Also known as... Commando Z!

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.990
It's... It's... It's...

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:37.300
IT'S ME!

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:43.640
God, seeing how pathetic a man my ancestor was moves me to tears!

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.140
Me?! Your...

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.140
ANCESTOR?!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:54.680
She got it! SHE GOT IT!

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.240
Oh, my, my, my!

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.150
Let me get this straight.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.160
You're my descendant, who's come from the future.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.420
And you make and sell the cyber dolls?

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.540
Have I got that right?

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:08.440
Yes!

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.370
That's about it.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:15.260
And while we're on the subject, you have no right to take such an arrogant tone with me!

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.670
You're a very rude little punk, kid!

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.740
You're the one who's being rude here, pal!

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.290
You're my descendant, which makes me your ancestor!

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.850
Show some respect!

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.780
Rest in peace, departed soul.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.200
Don't pray to me! That's bad luck!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.040
I meant speak politely to me! Politely!

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.270
Yes, sir! No, sir! Of course, sir!

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.560
No, <i>you</i> go, "Yes, sir! No, sir! Of course, sir!"

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.990
'Scuse me, Mr. President. What did you come here for?

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.160
SHUT UP!

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.710
And what's with that weird hair style?! It's lame!

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:47.810
Now you've done it!

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.250
Um, don't you want to ruin Saotome's day?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.760
SHUT UP!

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.080
And what's with that weirdo outfit?!

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.130
Stay away from me! SHIELDS UP!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.360
Well, I call DOUBLE shields up!

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.710
Dumbasses...

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.050
Hi, everyone! Gather around!

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.800
They're tickets to the amusement park, aren't they?

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:10.700
Yes! I won two tickets from the shopping raffle.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.520
Now, this first one

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.030
I'm giving to Kazuya as a present.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.020
Uh, thanks. Are you sure?

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.870
Yes, it's all right, Kazuya dear.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.530
Now, as for the remaining ticket...

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:26.530
What shall I do with this other ticket?

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.540
Who wants to go to the amusement park with Kazuya?

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.040
Me! Me! Me!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.140
Kazuya, here's your big chance.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.940
You can finally win my heart for yourself!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.090
Kazuya! Please help me with my research!

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:45.370
My research on human and cyber doll adrenalin secretion!

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.190
I want to see your adrenalin!

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:52.830
If we ride on thrill rides, I'm sure I'll be able to see it!

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:53.900
I'm scared of those rides—

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.350
Me, too!

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.810
I want to go to the amusement park with Kazuya!

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:03.220
Oh? Kasumi dear, don't you want the ticket as well?

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:06.490
I see. You obviously don't want it.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:11.040
Well, if you say so, how can I say no?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.800
Oh, my, my, my! I figured you'd try that.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:19.870
I'm sure you all realize there's only one ticket.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:24.840
So! I want you all to show me your true spirit!

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.900
Our spirit?

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.340
That's not scientific.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:28.320
Don't you see?

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:35.020
I'll give the ticket to whoever wants to go to the amusement park with Kazuya the most!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.690
Um, look, Mami—

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.960
Oh, my, my, my. Don't worry. Just be quiet and watch.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.190
Mmm, you little ladies man!

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.190
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:47.570
You speak politely to me!

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:52.540
You do it! You speak politely!

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.390
Hey! I heard it! It made a noise!

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:56.680
What're you talking about?! Don't be ridiculous!

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:58.100
This is so stupid.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.550
My job is to observe Saotome, so...

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:07.180
And now, the First Annual Mami Ticket Challenge Showdown!

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.300
The grand prize being...

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.850
THIS!

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.850
First challenge! A lightning round quiz!

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:15.880
I've got this!

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:19.580
No matter what questions come up,
my data base will have the answers!

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.360
Rena!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:26.780
Out with it. You always have it out when you think you'll lose.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.850
You noticed?

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.870
I'll do my best!

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.610
Oh... Subarashii!

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:40.520
The power of love is just filling this room!

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:44.460
Well, with that in mind, let's have question number one!

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:47.300
At the fish store in the Mt. Momiji shopping district,

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:52.000
the owner's youngest son, Yuji, will have a marriage meeting today.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.990
How many times has Yuji had these meetings?

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.900
Time's up!

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.300
The answer is 102!

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.600
And the fish there is always fresh and delicious!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.190
I don't know any of this!

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.400
Because it's nothing but neighborhood gossip!

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:14.910
Oh, my, my, my. Are these questions too hard? Well, then...

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.690
Time for the second challenge!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.990
All right! You can come out now!

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:25.090
I've just hidden the prize ticket
somewhere here in Kasumi House.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.800
So now it's a treasure hunt, right?

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.350
Yes! Finding it will take luck.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.590
And finders, keepers!

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.330
Oh, my, my, my.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.680
What are you doing?

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:49.330
I'm making a ticket detector.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:53.620
It'll take thirty minutes to design and two hours to build.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.300
Oh, my, my, my.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:59.890
May dear, what are you doing? Aren't you looking for it?

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.310
I can't help it. I have to clean up. It's my routine.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:03.290
Oh, my, my, my.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.050
What's this!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.800
No! Daimon left that over here!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.820
Pervert!

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.760
Repulsive!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.350
I'm innocent...

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.230
Kazuya dear...

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:21.330
Mami!

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:24.350
A healthy body should house healthy spirits as well.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.840
Hmm, naughty boy?

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.100
I'm telling you, it's not true!

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.610
Found it!

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.610
Th-That's Tadokoro's!

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.900
And here, too!

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:38.240
I'm keeping it for Prof. Yumi!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.750
By the way, everyone, haven't you gotten sidetracked?

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:48.950
Oh! You're right!

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.220
Yeah, the ticket...

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:51.830
It may be outside!

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.470
Kazuya.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:01.520
I'll clean it up, later. And besides that...

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.060
Besides that, I believe you!

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:07.200
Y-You're not listening to me.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:12.100
Sa-o-to-me?

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:12.940
Huh?

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:22.370
Shoubu ari!

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.870
I did it! I did it!

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.520
Saotome...

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.500
Let's have some fun together.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.580
What are you...

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.700
Hold it! She doesn't count!

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.250
I'm with Kasumi!

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.460
Yeah! Yeah!

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:37.700
Say what?! You wanna die right here and now or somethin'?!

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:39.270
I ain't givin' this ticket back!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.020
Hey! What's the big idea?!

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:44.940
Kasumi and the others do have a point.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:49.210
All right, I know! I'll take the ticket and run!

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:50.980
Whoever can get it away from me can keep it!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.360
Simple and straightforward.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.360
Oh, my, my, my. Here comes the final challenge!

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.610
What?!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:00.660
It's an emergency? That's the reason?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.560
Why you're here, kid?

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.980
Stop calling me kid!

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:20.000
That ramen wasn't enough?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.710
I never seem to have time to eat all I want lately.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:24.980
All right! Better recharge and refuel!

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.680
Pops! Gimme your biggest bowl!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.690
What are you doing?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.940
Plotting out Mami's movement route.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.130
She follows this route to go shopping every day.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.960
I'm sure she'll follow her routine...

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:40.260
so I'll ambush her.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.620
Oh, my, my, my!

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.620
At this rate, I'll never get Kazuya!

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.970
OVER HERE!

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.740
As I thought! You're following this course!

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.310
Well done, Kei dear.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.810
"Anticipation rules people," right?

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:13.800
Actually, I think the saying is "Anticipate to rule people."

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:16.820
But they also say that "Rules can ruin everything."

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.880
Which one is correct?

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:22.520
Oh, my, my, my.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:25.750
Gotcha!

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:26.930
Huh?

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.830
Not bad, May!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.330
N-Not bad yourself!

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.820
I'm not gonna lose!

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:36.860
Me, neither!

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.600
Here, that's sixth place for you.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.470
For Pete's sake...

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.060
All done!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.110
Huh? Miss, what's wrong?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.460
You usually eat thirty bowls.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:02.320
Not too hungry today. Sorry I can't finish it all.

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:18.500
May?

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.780
May!

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:23.010
Right! Just a second!

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.710
Make all the memories you can, okay?

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:27.350
Right!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.430
Because you don't have much time.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:34.190
She's right! It's already been twenty minutes.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:37.060
I've been waiting.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.590
R-Right. I'm coming...

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:43.200
You need a lot of time to get ready for a date, Kazuya dear.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.140
I guess you wouldn't know that.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:50.290
You're just like Takuya that way.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.040
With Mami not around, then...

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.540
My boots, my boots.

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.010
See you later!

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:01.590
See you when you get back!

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:09.280
Let's hit the field!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:17.730
Unlike Master Kotaro, Miss Chihiro's very fussy about food.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.880
Good morning, Sara! I've got the usual all ready!

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.700
What's wrong? You don't look well.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.610
Sara!

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.730
What's wrong?! Sara!

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.370
Too bad. Almost had it.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.260
One more time!

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:43.630
The coach is really into it today.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:47.130
Okay! That's it for today.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:19.330
Wishes do come true, don't they?

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:26.180
That other time, I wished in my heart that I could come back here with you.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.840
The first time we came here together?

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.100
And also...

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.060
What?

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:35.580
Never mind. It's nothing.

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.670
Stand up! Stand up, Sara!

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.650
What about our plans to make Saotome suffer?!

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:47.220
You aren't the one who's supposed to suffer!

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.320
Has it begun?

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.160
At last...

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:53.370
Whew! That was scary!

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:58.600
<i>I wish...</i>

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.470
Give me blood!

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:17.440
Kazuya!

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:18.900
Huh?

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:25.920
WHAT DID YOU SAY?!

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:27.390
Would you run that by me again?!

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:30.070
If worse comes to worst, we have to dissect Cyber Doll May!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:32.300
You... can't mean that.

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.830
Help yourself!

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.710
I got up before Mami and made it.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:41.200
Let's eat!

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:47.090
Oh, we forgot to pack a water bottle!

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.220
I'll go buy us one.

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:52.380
No, you keep eating.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:58.600
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:15:58.600 --> 00:15:59.870
<i>Juliano!</i>

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.310
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:03.950
<i>Juliano!</i>

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.360
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.560
<i>Juliano!</i>

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:11.070
N-No way...

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.930
That's impossible!

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:19.790
Mami, I think the shock was too much for Rena.

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:28.340
Rena, are you all right?

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.800
This isn't from shock.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:37.420
So, it's finally begun.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:38.780
Yo, guys!

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:45.850
Kazuya! Come on! Come on! Let's ride that next!

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.070
Don't be in such a rush. We have plenty of time.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:53.200
But I don't want to waste even a second of time I can be with you!

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.610
Come on! Come on!

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:03.080
What's with this fever?! What should we do?!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:05.670
For now, we need to cool them down.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.170
The rest is up to Kazuya.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.010
Okay, say cheese!

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:18.430
Mami!

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.980
What do I do? Somebody, help me!

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:23.680
Saotome! Saotome!

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:26.940
It's happening here, too. Where's Saotome?!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.900
The amusement park...

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:34.750
For the first time in his life,
Kotaro Nanbara begs for something.

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.160
Please... Please take care of Sara!

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:38.990
I'm going!

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:45.970
May...

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:46.750
Yes?

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.530
That time before, I also made a wish.

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:52.710
That I'd be able to ride this Ferris wheel again.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:57.260
Together with you, May.

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:00.760
Let's do this again!

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:04.470
Sure...

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:07.440
Sara! If you don't get back to normal,

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.650
I'll have to run my own errands!

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:14.280
I'm sorry!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.250
We almost got separated.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.360
Yeah...

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.030
For safety's sake.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.340
Right!

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:31.820
N-Nanbara?!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.350
Everyone's sick?!

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.840
Yeah. We don't know how to help them.

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.350
According to my incredibly rude descendant—

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.060
Descendant?

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.080
I'll explain later!

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:49.540
Anyway, according to him, apparently a virus is spreading.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.370
A virus fatal to cyber dolls!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:52.380
A virus?!

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:58.110
We cyber dolls have a self-evolving virus guard installed.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:01.100
I thought they were safe from viruses. So, why?

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:04.140
Like I know?! It's a hell of a virus!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.950
Kazuya!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.650
What took you so long?!

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:14.630
Shut up! I did my best!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.980
I'll explain later!

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:21.380
Their condition is stable, but it'll go critical if we don't do something.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:26.890
Is it true that, once the virus infects them, a cyber doll can't be reactivated?

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:31.390
I'm afraid so. It destroys all their memories.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:33.650
What happens when they're destroyed?!

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.100
If you view them as human,

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:37.880
it means that all the memories they have are gone.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:42.870
Personal experiences, knowledge, feelings... All memories.

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:45.700
For a cyber doll, it's the same as death.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:46.660
Death?!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.160
Oh, no.

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:51.330
What can we do?!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:53.950
I'll check out their systems! May!

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:54.740
Right!

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:04.890
I'll try to access deeper into it.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.080
This is the virus, huh?

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.140
Yeah...

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:14.830
How can we delete it?

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:16.740
How would I know?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.630
Why is May the only one...

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.230
Bingo! You got it.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:27.880
Cyber Doll May was returned to our company once already.

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:28.750
"Our" company?

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:29.610
Yes.

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:36.310
And when you reordered her, and we transferred her memories from that 1/6th scale body into this one,

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:38.420
an incredible discovery was made.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.890
Incredible discovery?

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:44.710
Yes. Cyber Doll May's system alone had undergone a subtle change.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.530
You've totally lost me.

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:48.260
Explain it more simply!

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:50.150
Think about it!

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:53.260
Does the software on your PC spontaneously change?

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.620
Of course not.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.560
Right. The same goes for robots.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:02.440
Once you program them, the program should be set for life.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.860
However, she completely astounded me.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:09.200
The program's growing!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.200
Then, the reason May isn't affected by the virus...

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.210
Right! Because it evolved inside of her!

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:19.100
If we can figure out how she's evolving,
we'd get a hint on how to design a vaccine program.

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:19.670
Maybe...

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.370
There's no "maybes" about it!

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:22.960
You guys built her, after all!

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:24.890
I'm afraid not.

00:21:24.890 --> 00:21:29.180
The MAID system, which forms the core OS of the cyber dolls,

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:31.350
was created by him!

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.560
That's why I came to ask you.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.980
The only person who can save the cyber dolls

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.990
is you, Kazuya Saotome!

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.250
Only you...

00:21:50.890 --> 00:22:00.000
Kimi no mae de mimi made akaku naru no wa

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:04.350
Doushite darou

00:22:04.350 --> 00:22:10.550
Futari-kiri wa nigatedashi

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:18.380
Oshaberi mo gikochinai

00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:25.530
Okashii yo ne ishiki shisugi

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:34.980
Kore ga koi na no? Sonna no zettai mitomenai

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:41.680
Sunao ni narenai sunao ni naritai

00:22:41.680 --> 00:22:48.360
Hontou no kimochi wa kokoro no naka

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:56.380
Itsuka kimi ga oshiete

00:22:58.390 --> 00:22:59.600
Nanbara here.

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:02.900
There's some confusion over May's catch-phrase "My best,"

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:05.450
causing many to mispronounce it as "My breasts."

00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:09.140
Now, one last time, let's hear you all say it loud and properly!

00:23:09.140 --> 00:23:09.950
Okay, all together now!

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:10.890
"My Best!"

00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:12.560
There! Well done!
